===============================================================================
MEDICAL DISCLAIMER
===============================================================================

This software is a research prototype. It is NOT a medical device, has NOT been
clinically validated, and must NOT be used to diagnose, treat, or make any
decision about a person's health.

Its measured melanoma recall on a held-out test set is 0.624 — roughly four in
ten melanomas are missed, and misses are frequently reported as benign lesions.
A confident output from this system is not evidence of a benign lesion. Any
concern about a skin lesion belongs with a qualified clinician.

===============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
===============================================================================

The MIT licence above covers the source code in this repository. It does NOT
cover the third-party content listed here, which carries its own terms.

--- HAM10000 dermoscopic images -------------------------------------------

Files:  samples/*.jpg (except cat.jpg), docs/class_samples_real.png

These are images from, or derived from, the HAM10000 dataset. HAM10000 is
distributed under a Creative Commons NonCommercial licence, which permits
redistribution with attribution for non-commercial use. Confirm the exact terms
against the canonical record before redistributing:

    Tschandl, P., Rosendahl, C. & Kittler, H. The HAM10000 dataset, a large
    collection of multi-source dermatoscopic images of common pigmented skin
    lesions. Sci. Data 5, 180161 (2018).
    https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2018.161

    Dataverse record: https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/DBW86T

The trained model weights in models/ are derived from this dataset and inherit
the same non-commercial restriction.

--- samples/cat.jpg -------------------------------------------------------

Provenance unknown. This file predates the current contributors' records and no
source or licence for it could be established. It serves only as a non-skin
control for the out-of-distribution gate and should be replaced with an image of
known provenance before any public redistribution.

--- Runtime dependencies --------------------------------------------------

Python packages are listed in requirements.txt and remain under their own
licences. The frontend loads Tailwind CSS, Google Material Symbols, and
html2pdf.js from public CDNs; none are vendored into this repository.
